nodecode-reachmap is a rewrite of MindSproutStudios's MindSproutStudios/hermes-reachmap:

  https://github.com/MindSproutStudios/hermes-reachmap
  commit f927ac96a63ecff6d7e614250d7a80b226f9a4b9
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 MindSprout Studios (LICENSE)

The plugin's scanners are here as Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell
contract: the DevTools probe that asks each browser on its port what it is
and which tabs it holds, the tab-to-service table, the sign-in read off a
page title, the listening-port and PATH scans, the MCP server list, the
drives, the capability tool and its find verb, the /reachmap command, the
denial matcher that catches a reply saying a reach is missing, and the
compact map frozen into each session's prompt. Each is reimplemented, not
translated: the scanners exchange JSON over loopback through nlk:http and
test a port with one TCP connect, so no Python, no Hermes runtime and no
plugin directory is needed.

Left out: the SQLite ledger of when each capability appeared and vanished
(its history readout and its rows per scan), the FastAPI web page and status
chip the plugin drew in Hermes's own UI, the Hermes credential store, and the
post-hook that rewrote a finished reply in place -- here the check answers
the model instead of editing it, since a Nodecode cell contributes a tool and
a prompt section rather than a message transform.
